{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01AaqYaPvApKeEh8PFXMe9T6", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://001.arktimes.com/?p=19804\"}, {\"url\": \"https://prod-ccroc-direct.merriam-webster.com/wordplay/what-does-wi-fi-really-mean\"}, {\"url\": \"https://monitor1.icoastalnet.com/?p=19804\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.mentalfloss.com/technology/what-does-wi-fi-stand-for\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.mentalfloss.com/posts/what-does-wi-fi-stand-for\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.corsair.com/ch/en/explorer/gamer/gaming-pcs/what-does-wi-fi-stand-for/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://wordsmarts.com/wi-fi-meaning/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.corsair.com/explorer/gamer/gaming-pcs/what-does-wi-fi-stand-for/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.corsair.com/pl/tw/explorer/gamer/gaming-pcs/what-does-wi-fi-stand-for/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://develop.wordsmarts.com/wi-fi-meaning\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:04:00.642Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Boing Boing Wi-Fi doesn't stand for anything letter from WECA first chairman", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_011hYuYKHB4fgcmkv9pCSe3b", "content": [{"title": "What Does Wi-Fi Actually Stand For? The Surprising Truth Behind the Name", "url": "https://001.arktimes.com/?p=19804"}, {"title": "What Does 'Wi-Fi' Really Mean?", "url": "https://prod-ccroc-direct.merriam-webster.com/wordplay/what-does-wi-fi-really-mean"}, {"title": "monitor1.icoastalnet.com", "url": "https://monitor1.icoastalnet.com/?p=19804"}, {"title": "what does wi fi stand for", "url": "https://www.mentalfloss.com/technology/what-does-wi-fi-stand-for"}, {"title": "What Does ‘Wi-Fi’ Stand For? It’s Complicated", "url": "https://www.mentalfloss.com/posts/what-does-wi-fi-stand-for"}, {"title": "what does wi fi stand for", "url": "https://www.corsair.com/ch/en/explorer/gamer/gaming-pcs/what-does-wi-fi-stand-for/"}, {"title": "person using computer laptop with Wi-Fi 7", "url": "https://wordsmarts.com/wi-fi-meaning/"}, {"title": "what does wi fi stand for", "url": "https://www.corsair.com/explorer/gamer/gaming-pcs/what-does-wi-fi-stand-for/"}, {"title": "what does wi fi stand for", "url": "https://www.corsair.com/pl/tw/explorer/gamer/gaming-pcs/what-does-wi-fi-stand-for/"}, {"title": "person using computer laptop with Wi-Fi 7", "url": "https://develop.wordsmarts.com/wi-fi-meaning"}]}, "The search didn't turn up a letter from WECA's first chairman. What it did find is a related statement from a WECA co-founder, Phil Belanger, who said the name has no meaning. Several sources date the name's origin to 1999 and credit the branding agency Interbrand.\n\n- **Belanger's statement:** One source describes him as a founding member of WECA who presided over the selection of the title. Another says he told Boing Boing's Cory Doctorow in 2005 that some colleagues worried people would want a literal explanation for the name (\"some of my colleagues were afraid … They could not imagine using the name 'Wi-Fi' without having some sort of literal explanation.\"). I didn't find a published letter, and none of the sources call him the first chairman.\n- **Origin:** The term Wi-Fi was created by the brand consulting firm Interbrand in 1999. Sources also say WECA enlisted the marketing agency Interbrand to rename it.\n- **Common myth:** The \"Wireless Fidelity\" expansion is widely repeated, but the Oxford English Dictionary calls that rationalization \"spurious.\"\n\nFor the exact wording of the letter or Belanger's formal role, the original Boing Boing piece from 2005 would be the best place to check."], "durationSeconds": 6.378477667000001, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01AaqYaPvApKeEh8PFXMe9T6", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
