{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_0129WauZJydYpJDFQ6zoHZCp", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for-.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://blogs.arubanetworks.com/?p=8975\"}, {\"url\": \"https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for.html/amp\"}, {\"url\": \"https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for-.html/amp\"}, {\"url\": \"https://community.hpe.com/t5/networking/what-does-wi-fi-stand-for/ba-p/7218970\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.mentalfloss.com/technology/what-does-wi-fi-stand-for\"}, {\"url\": \"https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for-html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://etymologist.ai/word/wifi\"}, {\"url\": \"https://lr.eu.psf.lt/r/Jeopardy/comments/1dv5uvm/wifi_means_nothing\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:04:14.745Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Phil Belanger WECA first chairman Wi-Fi Alliance Boing Boing 2005 \"Wi-Fi\" doesn't stand for anything", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_018R3doGdDAruSrFTmrVXH47", "content": [{"title": "wifi isnt short for", "url": "https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for.html"}, {"title": "wifi isnt short for", "url": "https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for-.html"}, {"title": "blogs.arubanetworks.com", "url": "https://blogs.arubanetworks.com/?p=8975"}, {"title": "boingboing.net", "url": "https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for.html/amp"}, {"title": "boingboing.net", "url": "https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for-.html/amp"}, {"title": "- Community Home", "url": "https://community.hpe.com/t5/networking/what-does-wi-fi-stand-for/ba-p/7218970"}, {"title": "what does wi fi stand for", "url": "https://www.mentalfloss.com/technology/what-does-wi-fi-stand-for"}, {"title": "wifi isnt short for html", "url": "https://boingboing.net/2005/11/08/wifi-isnt-short-for-html"}, {"title": "etymologist.ai", "url": "https://etymologist.ai/word/wifi"}, {"title": "r/Jeopardy Jul 04 '24", "url": "https://lr.eu.psf.lt/r/Jeopardy/comments/1dv5uvm/wifi_means_nothing"}]}, "The search turned up the 2005 Boing Boing post and several later sources that repeat Belanger's account.\n\n- **The Boing Boing post (November 2005):** It ran a Belanger statement, which he gave as a founding member of the Wi-Fi Alliance who oversaw choosing the name. He said the name has no meaning and isn't an acronym. The post also says the Interbrand firm created the name and the yin-yang logo, choosing from a list of 10 proposals. Belanger's statement: the name is not an acronym and has no meaning. Interbrand invented the name and the logo.\n- **The tagline:** Belanger said the \"Wireless Fidelity\" idea came from a tagline. The initial six-member board invented that tagline, which he says means nothing either. The alliance later dropped it once marketing and business people from larger companies joined the board.\n- **Origin of the name:** A 2025-era Mental Floss piece quotes Belanger, who was a co-founder of the Wireless Ethernet Compatibility Alliance (WECA, now the Wi-Fi Alliance). The standard was known as 802.11, which was hard to say, so WECA hired Interbrand to rename it. In Belanger's words, the team had been hired to find a name and logo for interoperability seal and marketing efforts, something catchier than \"IEEE 802.11b Direct Sequence.\"\n- **Caveat on the \"Wireless Fidelity\" link:** Belanger's account says the phrase only spread because some colleagues worried the name needed an explanation. He says the only reason anyone hears about \"Wireless Fidelity\" is that some colleagues were afraid.\n\nThe Boing Boing post also contains Belanger's text, so the quotes are from a primary-adjacent source. Mental Floss and the Aruba and HPE community reposts are secondary, and the etymologist.ai page and a Reddit thread are weaker sources, though the Reddit thread points back to the Boing Boing post."], "durationSeconds": 8.570795167, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_0129WauZJydYpJDFQ6zoHZCp", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
